window.LEARN = {"projects":[["badnorth","Bad North 2017–19"],["townscaper","Townscaper 2019–21"],["next","第三项目 2021–25"],["other","其他"]],"topics":[["water","水 / 岸线"],["grid","网格 / 拓扑"],["light","光照 / 阴影"],["terrain","地形 / 岛屿"],["build","建筑 / 模块"],["life","植被 / 生物 / 装饰"],["texture","贴图 / 风格"],["fx","Bad North 玩法 / 特效"],["tools","UI / 工具 / 工程"],["show","展示 / 无技术说明"]],"labels":{"done":"重构版已实现","game":"已用于 Townscaper","engine":"已在 engine 实现","both":"两边都用了","partial":"部分实现","ref":"学习参考","todo":"未实现","na":"与项目无关"},"items":[{"id":"1995813566344011807","date":"2025-12-02","text":"I'm designing a jungle gym / climbable shelf structure for the play area of our home. The sofa-like structure to the left is folding mattress you can slide under the monkey bars. If you've ever build something similar I'd be happy to take advice","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"家里的攀爬架，与游戏无关","project":"other"},{"id":"1991103578011029507","date":"2025-11-19","text":"I think it gives a pretty good sense of a dynamic ocean without being too distractive","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/world/view.js / engine/waves.js","note":"动态海面但不抢戏：极低幅度的颜色漂移","project":"next"},{"id":"1991101097818403263","date":"2025-11-19","text":"It's based on a looping vertex shader. The data is baked at generation-time. Each vert has an in-direction, an out-direction and a time offset.","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/water/shore.js / engine/waves.js","note":"循环顶点着色器；生成时烘焙：每个顶点存入射点、出射点、时间偏移。讨论串：\"没有整块海面网格\"、\"浪会反弹\"","project":"next"},{"id":"1991099314714902634","date":"2025-11-19","text":"Got some pretty sweet new shore waves going","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/water/shore.js / engine/waves.js","note":"新的岸边浪","project":"next"},{"id":"1897266928961700215","date":"2025-03-05","text":"Yet another hallway design","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"other"},{"id":"1890018647655272491","date":"2025-02-13","text":"Further iterations on hallway design","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"other"},{"id":"1852334860137849222","date":"2024-11-01","text":"A fluffy cloud shader. It is using the same impostors as the trees, in case that isn't obvious.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/impostor.js","note":"同一个烘焙器烘一团白色云团块；实例放大、alpha 用 smoothstep 做软边、底部偏灰、沿风向在着色器里慢慢飘","project":"next"},{"id":"1849732997945110651","date":"2024-10-25","text":"Here, the shoreline is shown in yellow. A pushed out and smoothed shoreline is shown in blue. The waves travel from the blue line to the yellow (and back a little). There is also a global water mask texture that adds extra foam around rocks and stuff.","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/water/shore.js / engine/waves.js","note":"黄线=岸线，蓝线=外推并平滑的岸线；浪从蓝走到黄再退回一点","project":"next"},{"id":"1849730611964973481","date":"2024-10-25","text":"Shoreline waves! This is something I've tackled many times. Although this one is very subtle, it's my favorite thus far. Instead of trying to make the waves roll in and out inside one shader pass, I'm creating loads of overlapping waves that each go through their own cycle","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/water/shore.js / engine/waves.js","note":"很多条重叠的浪，每条有自己的周期，而不是一个 pass 里整体涨落","project":"next"},{"id":"1849427564034498642","date":"2024-10-24","text":"Made some octagonal impostors for these trees. Might seem like overkill for such a stylized look, but they're a lot more stable when rotating the camera than all other billboard solutions I've tried, which is kinda important.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/impostor.js","note":"8 个水平方位（每 45°）各烘一张进图集；每棵树一个只绕 Y 轴的四边形，按\"镜头相对这棵树朝向的方位角\"取相邻两张按角度混合 → 转镜头稳定；alpha 边缘一圈墨色","project":"next"},{"id":"1798310423554658732","date":"2024-06-05","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1795831296952041691","date":"2024-05-29","text":"I'm putting together a navigation structure that lets you travel faster along rivers (and especially downstream)","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/world/navgraph.js","note":"河上的边更便宜，顺流最快","project":"next"},{"id":"1791049306213912823","date":"2024-05-16","text":"Trying out a new lighting solution. This one is just one lookup in the vertex shader of a low res cube map height map.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1786014232594485497","date":"2024-05-02","text":"Mountain textures! These have been tricky. Mountains kinda need lighting and normals, but with my texture blending tech I don't think I can afford that on low-end devices","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1783792917183606829","date":"2024-04-26","text":"Texture test!","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1781405550061687016","date":"2024-04-19","text":"Ok this might not look like much but I've got seamless patch blending! Some of the patches are projected (like the grass and the water) and some are manually UV-mapped (like the shoreline). With some good textures and some height based blending this is gonna be great.","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"顶面画成扇形：中心本格颜色，角上取\"共用此角、同高度、非河道\"的所有顶面颜色平均 → 草 / 苔 / 沙之间无缝过渡","project":"next"},{"id":"1769691526924292506","date":"2024-03-18","text":"Mega river system! I've had trouble making good rivers before. Now I've sort of special cased the rivers by collapsing them depth-first to let them wiggle real far, and then the rest is collapsed breadth-first, making nice gentle slopes that only occasionally meet steep cliffs.","topic":"terrain","status":"engine","where":"engine/rivers.js","note":"河流深度优先坍缩、其余广度优先成缓坡","project":"next"},{"id":"1769641473895432220","date":"2024-03-18","text":"In cute tile based planets like this you often get a \"mushrooming\" issue where tall mountains get weirdly wide. I managed to mitigate this by a relax pass where all module-containing cells try to achieve their desired shape and size. Note the cells on the top left contracting.","topic":"grid","status":"engine","where":"engine/relax.js","note":"蘑菇化：relax 让含模块的格子趋向期望大小","project":"next"},{"id":"1768627849529893109","date":"2024-03-15","text":"For reasons I will not be explaining at this point I've gone and put this on a sphere","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1765115069837221962","date":"2024-03-05","text":"Here, I'm visualizing the recursive tree parsing as it adds new rects. Note that when the board is more fragmented the arm tends to have more fingers.","topic":"life","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1765041830461055127","date":"2024-03-05","text":"Now supports removing rects too! The bin space gets quite fragmented after a while though.. I've tried to optimize it on the fly but I can't figure out how to when it get sort of interlocked. Still packs tight though!","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1764958522398146667","date":"2024-03-05","text":"A cute binary tree rect packer. Generating the placement attempts is kinda brute force (to get into all the nooks and crannies), but then it's using the tree properly for fast collision checks. I think this is the first time I've actually written a proper space partion tree. Fun.","topic":"life","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1758251637280268481","date":"2024-02-15","text":"It's simply a stack of planes sampling an SDF I had laying around. Gives a much more fluid vibe than the basic flipped mesh approach in Bad North and Townscaper","topic":"water","status":"engine","where":"engine/watervol.js","note":"一叠平面采样 SDF 做水面反射","project":"next"},{"id":"1758250248483278925","date":"2024-02-15","text":"New water reflection I'm quite happy with","topic":"water","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1751945034851570056","date":"2024-01-29","text":"Some nice new highlights when the island is backlit. Achieved by simply adding another inverted mesh outline layer that shows up when looking into the sun. And masked by shadows, of course.","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/world/outline.js","note":"两层反向外壳：墨线（固定像素宽）+ 更宽的逆光亮边，只在镜头朝太阳、迎光一侧出现；阴影遮罩用朝下程度近似","project":"next"},{"id":"1751932427272909032","date":"2024-01-29","text":"I can now force specific modules to appear. To do this I first generate the specific bit of grid they need. A large module like this would be highly unlikely to appear by chance on a random grid.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js（forceChurch）","note":"强制模块：先压平台地，再放教堂（中殿 + 钟楼）","project":"next"},{"id":"1727324352264474664","date":"2023-11-22","text":"Yeah that actually looks pretty good. I did not expect that.","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1727315611959865407","date":"2023-11-22","text":"I've shipped two whole games with orbital cameras and not once have I previously though about adding motion blur smear. What a fool I am.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1724449858369568780","date":"2023-11-14","text":"Ok, here's a small example. The button toggles a ScriptableObject bool. The FloatSelectNode component listens to that ScriptableObject, and then a series of node-like components end up moving a piece of UI","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1714613599035863191","date":"2023-10-18","text":"Another strange texturing style. This time trying to look a bit like abstract fields. A nice thing is they show the game tiles quite clearly. In the end I probably want a mix where some areas are more man made and others more natural.","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1712088611934371876","date":"2023-10-11","text":"Another take on a palette authoring tool","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1710031224838771027","date":"2023-10-05","text":"Ok here's a probably horrible way to author color volumes. The idea is to properly define the whole color possibility space for each feature","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1708815475801505819","date":"2023-10-02","text":"a cool cliff I came across","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js","note":"海中石柱：浪蚀台脚 + 蘑菇帽","project":"next"},{"id":"1707497006640365880","date":"2023-09-28","text":"And here's a couple more being generated","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1707490932017279035","date":"2023-09-28","text":"They are of course 100% texture, painted onto a fairly low, poly mesh. I keep thinking I'm gonna need to give em some volume with billboard sprites, but now I'm not so sure anymore. Especially with the lil' shadows, they look quite volumetric as they are.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1707490274425884929","date":"2023-09-28","text":"I added back the lil' shrubbery at the edges of things for like the 3rd time","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"崖顶线（顶面边上邻居更低）每隔一段一丛灌木，往里收一点；颜色大多绿，少数橄榄 / 赭色","project":"next"},{"id":"1705195380457996629","date":"2023-09-22","text":"I tamed the texture based surface shadows a bit, so the shadow casting height is independent of the z test height. Now I only get shadows over grass-cliff edges and under roofs. It has some artifacts across UV borders, but it's quite subtle so I might not actually have to fix it.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1704246032626762189","date":"2023-09-19","text":"Ok, I think maybe this is a bit of a sweet spot. It's got a nice variable density texture to it. There are some height segmentation lines to help with readability, but they don't feel too synthetic.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1704218784028905984","date":"2023-09-19","text":"I tried some texture based shadows. Note the shadows on the grass and along the roof edges. Looks kinda cool, but feels a bit too 3D for what I'm going for this time. I feel like it clashes with lines, and I like lines more.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1703750394164199473","date":"2023-09-18","text":"Looking at my procedural stylized ground texturing again. Really like the swirly blobbyness of these. They feel kind of damp for some reason.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1699146321318314094","date":"2023-09-05","text":"Oh! And now I finally figured out how to make non-straight sedimentary lines! Most of the texturing math is kinda linear, so I though the lines had to be linear too. But I could (obviously) just make the whole world wobbly, do the texturing math, then simply undo the wobble.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"把世界弄弯、算贴图、再弯回去：沉积线高度 = 层中线 + 世界空间噪声(x,z)，相邻崖面同一噪声 → 连续起伏的岩层","project":"next"},{"id":"1699038611125985317","date":"2023-09-05","text":"Looking att sedimentation lines again. Helps make large cliffs more interesting. Also makes their shape a bit more readable maybe.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"沉积线让大崖壁更耐看、形体更好读：每层一条，贴在崖面外侧","project":"next"},{"id":"1696896119794479541","date":"2023-08-30","text":"On the other hand, I've always wanted to make a game in the Art Nouveau style. This might be a good fit. Look how neat and controlled the grass blotches bleed over the cliff edges.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/terrainmesh.js","note":"草顶面、邻居更低的边：沿崖面往下垂一段圆润的草色舌头，深度 = 噪声 × sin(πu)^0.6，不是每段都有","project":"next"},{"id":"1696864977171189980","date":"2023-08-30","text":"I'm slowly emerging from a huge refactoring... While this here is not exactly the look I'm going for, it's showing off a big improvement to the texturing. I'm now able to draw with much bigger blotches without the blotches bleeding across and messing up important edges.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1677242779162877952","date":"2023-07-07","text":"I am (once again) rewriting my generic triangle graph system to (hopefully) be more robust and generic. Here's a stress test where I'm adding random verts, making sure the graph stays mainifold and delauney-ish along the way.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1671840905957978113","date":"2023-06-22","text":"Hmm.. I thought it was gonna be too wacky but maybe it's kinda cool","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1671808851895627776","date":"2023-06-22","text":"If your terrain generator supports overhangs you gotta flaunt it. I don't make the rules, but I do follow them.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js · terrainmesh.js","note":"悬垂：崖顶外伸、底下空、下面的地照样画","project":"next"},{"id":"1670794261669769217","date":"2023-06-19","text":"Oh, and I finally got this lovely rock feature to show up! When working with WFC, sometimes you build a cool tile and it wont show up in forever, since it's conditions are so specific. You forget about it, and then suddenly: poof!","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/features.js","note":"天然石拱","project":"next"},{"id":"1670790425232175108","date":"2023-06-19","text":"I'm prepping for a talk in Cambridge next week, thus all the gifs. I made my generator also output pure triangle/hex and square grids, to illustrate why I'm going for my mixed approach.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1670725072540106755","date":"2023-06-19","text":"Here's a comparison showing no-, dumb- and hierarchical smoothing. The hierarchical smoothing helps preserve the intent of the input-tiles while smoothing out the jankyness from the weird underlying grid and from the limited slope angles in the input tileset","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"对比三种：不平滑 / dumb（海岸被啃、崖顶塌）/ 层级（海岸圆滑、崖顶与房子保持锐利）。「地形」场景勾掉「层级平滑」即可对比","project":"next"},{"id":"1670720537662836736","date":"2023-06-19","text":"I smooth my mesh according to an edge type hierarchy. Black is hard, red is game-tile-border and blue is material-border. Verts only get to pull at equal or lower order verts, and only along the appropriate edges","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"切面上分级：钉住(外圈/房子 tile/分叉点) > 崖顶线 > 崖脚线 > 内部；轮廓点只沿同级边、只被同级或更高级拉（Taubin 不缩），内部点吸收位移。画面里黑=硬、红=tile 边、蓝=材质边","project":"next"},{"id":"1670064751181791233","date":"2023-06-17","text":"I figured out how to mimic Thread.Sleep() in Burst! Just store time in a static unsafe NativeArray! Then you can write to it from the main thread and read from it inside a job! Probably super bad in many ways but good enough for visualization and debug!","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1669315384619540487","date":"2023-06-15","text":"The generator consistently spits out pretty cool islands now","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1666429884208381953","date":"2023-06-07","text":"I've been banging my head against various shore line rendering options for a good week now. Gonna stick with this for now I think, which is basically just a refined version of what I did for Bad North and Townscaper.","topic":"water","status":"ref","where":"src/water/shore.js","note":"BN/Townscaper 岸线方案的精修版，作为参数对照","project":"next"},{"id":"1664566546683899905","date":"2023-06-02","text":"Here's a distance field-like mesh skirt solution very similar to Townscaper and Bad North. It works for calm waters I guess... But I would like something with a bit more punch this time. A bit more crashing waves.","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/water/shore.js / engine/shorefield.js","note":"类距离场的浪裙：栅格化陆地 + chamfer 距离，外推点按真实距离放置，海湾不会折叠","project":"next"},{"id":"1664565063552847873","date":"2023-06-02","text":"I'm trying out using a shader based fluid simulation. But I'm skeptical. It seems to need 32 bit float render targets, and I don't trust that those will work across platforms. Might also be a challenge to tweak, stylize, and feed back to CPU if needed.","topic":"water","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1654401054828638214","date":"2023-05-05","text":"An quaint island being procedurally generated","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1593215065423245313","date":"2022-11-17","text":"Making a lil dynamic sprite packer, able to add and remove sprite allotments at runtime. I had one of these in Bad North and found it very useful. Here, the sprites are baked live from meshes. So I guess it's basically impostors. Though I expect to use it for much else too.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/core/atlas.js","note":"二叉树矩形打包：按剩余较多的方向切；free() 后兄弟都空就向上合并；impostor 烘焙从这里分配格子","project":"next"},{"id":"1590674061092212738","date":"2022-11-10","text":"In the vertex shader, my grass gets to sample that contrast texture both where they stand, and also raycast into the background. The outline strength is determined by the difference between these two samples! Not perfect, but pretty good! Not too jittery when turning the camera","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"背景反差近似：草丛离\"邻居更低\"的边 < 0.11 → aEdge=1，画一层加宽、后推的墨色草丛；平地中间的草没有墨线","project":"next"},{"id":"1590669875869286400","date":"2022-11-10","text":"An early look at grass billboards. I really like how they add a completely new kind of shape and detail frequency.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"草丛广告牌：只绕 Y 轴转向镜头，顶部随风摆、颜色变浅；草 / 苔顶面上撒，坡上更密","project":"next"},{"id":"1584623053061099520","date":"2022-10-24","text":"I wrote a thing to splice houses into the terrain. Mostly, the houses are part of pre-build tiles, but would be useful insert them at will too. You can kinda see the structure of my mesh system and mesh algoritms by how the yellow lines are rotating around the verts.","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1582757294672314368","date":"2022-10-19","text":"I'm seeing if my light volume approach can work with point lights too. The low resolution is noticeable for sure. Especially when you move em around like this. But if you keep em big and soft and somewhat still I think it's gonna be good.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1582293326815862786","date":"2022-10-18","text":"I thought it would be too expensive to properly evaluate each tile placement. But! While the number of possible tiles is indeed very large, it is actually quite small around the collapsed edge! Thus, my algorithm now tries to expand (and interconnect) a simplified nav graph.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/world/navgraph.js","note":"简化导航图：同高连片 = 区域节点，Dijkstra 最短路树","project":"next"},{"id":"1580846877855338497","date":"2022-10-14","text":"Here's the slowed down bounce sequence. You can see how the mega texture and the light volume affect each other back and forth. After about the 3rd bounce, further bounces are not noticeable.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1580845127207387137","date":"2022-10-14","text":"1st texture here is an sdf volume. The distance lives in the alpha, but RG actually reference UVs in the mega texture! 2nd is a baked 6 directional light volume, raycast against the sdf, sampling the mega texture using the UVs where it hits the sdf. 3rd is the lit mega texture","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1580835075629133825","date":"2022-10-14","text":"I always write my own lighting solutions. I've had some really naive ad hoc color bleeding in my (very fake) GI before, but this is my first decent attempt to actually have the light *bounce*","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1580162341668237312","date":"2022-10-12","text":"I start with a very basic Marching Cubes mesh from a bunch of spheres. I mark the edges between triangles that are closest to different spheres. Then I run an iterative relax algorithm where those hard edges are like rubber bands, and the rest is sort of a like a balloon.","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"团块的轮廓用反向外壳墨线（跟随「墨线」开关）；原片是在三角形之间标边","project":"next"},{"id":"1580158269267406849","date":"2022-10-12","text":"Can you make good looking foliage from Marching Cubes-blobs? Maybe?","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"树冠 = 几个球融在一起，法线取离整团中心的方向与自身法线的混合 → 像 Marching Cubes 团块一样整团受光；三种树冠变体","project":"next"},{"id":"1579483114178768898","date":"2022-10-10","text":"Obviously, it's all tile-based. I went through a major rewrite to combine an irregular grid (like in Townscaper) with multi-cell tiles (like in Bad North). Note how one of the house tiles even cover both a square tile AND a triangular tile","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js · core/grid.js","note":"多格 tile：同一栋房子相邻格之间不起墙，三角格 + 方格拼一栋","project":"next"},{"id":"1579478470098243584","date":"2022-10-10","text":"To make the cliffs look more organic, I'm doing some pretty radical cage deformation on the cells.","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/terrain/shape.js","note":"笼形变形：崖顶线沿外法线随高度内收（下宽上窄），加随高度缓变的噪声让崖壁扭动；位移有上限防翻折","project":"next"},{"id":"1579474420749725696","date":"2022-10-10","text":"I'm back on the island generation","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1490068909042642944","date":"2022-02-05","text":"Late night cryptic graph tweet","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1489193847422865410","date":"2022-02-03","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1482346496460828674","date":"2022-01-15","text":"I created a dedicated contrast texture system for the lines: an iterative simulation on the triangles that starts random and then tries to make contrasted edges different, and non-contrasted edges similar. A byproduct is a beautiful color gradient that help express connectivity","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1482011744843223042","date":"2022-01-14","text":"Ok, I stumbled on a pretty cool art style now. Here, I'm creating pixel thin lines from contrasts in my procedural normal map. I should probably move to a bespoke contrast texture (to get more deliberate control over the lines). But I gotta say this looks pretty promising.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1481661852887265288","date":"2022-01-13","text":"Yet another light baker. Actually does some ray marching, but still pretty ad hoc. The textures are: 1. Normals (procedurally painted in big chunky strokes) 2. 3D Signed Distance Field 3. 3D Ambient Occlusion in positive and negative X,Y and Z","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1480635131614355459","date":"2022-01-10","text":"More experiments in procedural texturing of procedural islands. Still very early, but I do like these big paint blotches. They hide the polys well and they would be hard to achieve with other means. Definitely need a proper lighting system though. And probably some outlines.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1478114309263839244","date":"2022-01-03","text":"Yeah that's good enough for now. I quite like how the radial (instead of directional) size-sorting looks. Gonna make for some visually pleasing textures with that big coherent chunk in the middle.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1471817524148940807","date":"2021-12-17","text":"Some rocky islands. Trying to make the grid natural and readable, yet funky. Square, yet hex.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1466059785703460870","date":"2021-12-01","text":"Oh. What's this? A free Townscaper web demo, playable straight in the browser: http:// oskarstalberg.com/Townscaper/ 🕊️💦🌊🏡🏤⛪️🏤🏡🌊💦🕊️","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1459169210752507904","date":"2021-11-12","text":"And another","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1458921394855718917","date":"2021-11-11","text":"I'm exploring the Half Edge data structure. Feels like a really lightweight, powerful and versatile way of representing topology. A big thanks to everyone suggesting I look into it.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1448039167057879048","date":"2021-10-12","text":"Imma talk about my new island generator at Sweden Game Conference (@SwedenGameArena) on Friday (no idea if its gonna be recorded). Naturally, I'm preparing by implementing some nice timing and visualization.","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1447496205282549761","date":"2021-10-11","text":"The base graph is just a humble irregular triangle grid","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1447494168448753667","date":"2021-10-11","text":"Long time fans of the show will not be surprised to learn that this is indeed running on tile based WFC. This time around, I'm getting the best of both worlds by using a mix of triangular and square tiles. (The squares are cut along each diagonal to create 4 triangles though)","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1447488323845509121","date":"2021-10-11","text":"I'm able to do a couple of things here I've always wanted to, but never been able to before: - Properly combine seamless soft slopes with distinct sharp cliffs. - Erosion valid terrain with no local minimums. - Get the best of both square tiles and triangular tiles","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1447483550257799171","date":"2021-10-11","text":"I regret to inform you that I've relapsed into procedural island generation","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"next"},{"id":"1430227487376781317","date":"2021-08-24","text":"Plus you can change the in-game textures now! So I guess the game is now (in the most liberal use of the word) \"moddable\"","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1430224300003545091","date":"2021-08-24","text":"If you've been waiting for the Townscaper mesh exporter, you can now try it out in the public beta branch on Steam. There's a bunch of other subtle changes and optimizations too, but nothing major. Please do let me know if you run into any issues!","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1427721874490933250","date":"2021-08-17","text":"Here's a very quick technical test. Though this one is continuously adding decals, so it looks a bit like claymation or line boil. Might be softer than what I'd be going for, but it was an easy style to throw together. And obviously you'd need some padding for the seams.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1410697531424714752","date":"2021-07-01","text":"Townscaper is now on GoG! https:// gog.com/game/townscaper","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1401145625572425728","date":"2021-06-05","text":"Meshes in Townscaper are kept small to rely on Unity's dynamic mesh batching. This approach was not performant enough on the Switch though, so I wrote a mesh merger to do my own batching instead. It made a huge difference, something like tripling the rendering speed.","topic":"tools","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"整城合并成一个网格一次 draw call（倒影复用同一份几何）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1384958097542819845","date":"2021-04-21","text":"I wrote a script to trace topologically straight lines across the Townscaper grid. I think I'll use it for a thing in the gamepad controls and possibly some drag-to-paint mode.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1371460793032716290","date":"2021-03-15","text":"I got it working within the duration of exactly 1 kid nap","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1371191380773629956","date":"2021-03-14","text":"Yeah this is gonna be pretty good","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1370772056279805953","date":"2021-03-13","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1344290848180203523","date":"2020-12-30","text":"A rare look at Townscapers sophisticated QA process","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1338829205157646336","date":"2020-12-15","text":"Apparently, one way to do Delaunay Triangulation on a sphere is to do it on a Stereographic Projection. (Many people have done this before me, so it's nothing new). My points are sorted vertically, which means radially, which makes the algorithm faster. Here's what it looks like:","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1338825080844021760","date":"2020-12-15","text":"Apropos of nothing, a take on the ancient issue of generating nice triangulated spheres 1. Random points 2. Space out the points 3. Triangulate 4. Relax using the triangles Unclear if I'll use this for anything helpful sources: https:// redblobgames.com/x/1842-delauna y-voronoi-sphere/ … https:// newcastle.edu.au/__data/assets/ pdf_file/0017/22508/13_A-fast-algorithm-for-constructing-Delaunay-triangulations-in-the-plane.pdf …","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1332410042784641026","date":"2020-11-27","text":"How the infinite grid is relaxed and kept seamless: The grid is made of Patches. Adjacent triplets form Clusters. Clusters and Patches are relaxed independently. Each Vert is a triangular interpolation its representation in the closest 2 Clusters and the Patch wherein it sits.","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/core/grid.js","note":"Patch / Cluster 三角插值拼接未做；当前把六边形外圈钉住保证轮廓","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1331905048801144836","date":"2020-11-26","text":"Townscaper now has lighthouses! This pattern required more code rewrite than seems reasonable. Luckily, I got some slight optimization out of it too. https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1313841094069817344","date":"2020-10-07","text":"Because I'm quite proud of my lighting (and because Townscaper is basically just a tech demo anyway) I added texture-only and light-only render modes","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"只看贴图 / 只看光照两种渲染模式","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1313840428685447170","date":"2020-10-07","text":"I added some sunlight (with shadows) and a gizmo to control it","topic":"light","status":"partial","where":"src/world/view.js setTimeOfDay","note":"太阳光 + 阴影；夜里窗户亮。做了白天/黄昏/夜晚三档（N 键），没做可拖动的太阳小部件","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1313837640366596096","date":"2020-10-07","text":"I just pushed an update to Townscaper. You can now build flying towns (if you find any of the perfect loops I've scattered across the grid) https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1310503825510367232","date":"2020-09-28","text":"Ok, I tried the mixed perspective. Note how houses further away are smaller, yet the vertical lines stay straight and parallel. It's definitely not a good fit for Townscaper, but might work well if I make another Bad North-ish game with a hearty mix of 3D meshes and billboards.","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1305951750638231552","date":"2020-09-15","text":"To soften it up a bit, I'm trying out a penumbra approach where I draw the shadow thrice, once normal, once pulled in slightly and once with big voxels. I think I like it. (here, the shadow is shown darker than it should be to demonstrate the effect)","topic":"light","status":"partial","where":"src/world/view.js","note":"三次绘制做半影未做，用 PCFSoft 近似","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1305948413872267265","date":"2020-09-15","text":"I'm exploring cast shadows. They have to be quite subtle and soft to fit the style. It does seems like they should be fast enough for mobile too if I only update them on command after a regeneration.","topic":"light","status":"game","where":"src/world/view.js","note":"柔和投影：实时 PCF 软阴影，海面有投影接收层","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1302686201401442309","date":"2020-09-06","text":"A smoothing and inversion bug I came across while playing with the grid generation. The inverted patches collapse into a mess, but are stretched out when interpolating to fit with their neighbors. And the poor non-inverted patches need to stretch real far to pick up the slack","topic":"grid","status":"game","where":"src/core/grid.js","note":"反转/凹格问题：新网格逐格做凸性统计，2516 格中 0 个凹四边形","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1301816247479345152","date":"2020-09-04","text":"Some are asking for the option to use regular grids. Now, that's (obviously) against the Townscaper design philosophy. However, I am thinking of sprinkling the current generated grid with random patches of hand crafted grid, like little gems to find and build your tempels upon","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1298689301488775169","date":"2020-08-26","text":"Flat texture, shaded, lighting only, and my AO baking mesh. I'm thinking of adding some little widgets like this to give people a peek at how things work. Perhaps hide them behind a break-glass-to-push-button widget.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"平贴图 / 着色 / 只看光照 / AO 烘焙网格四种调试视图","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1290997501332525056","date":"2020-08-05","text":"#Townscaper is now properly released on Mac on Steam! To celebrate the occasion, I added some garden paths. Go get it: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"后院 ≥6 格时按格心协方差求主轴，离主轴（和副轴）< 0.2 的格子铺浅色石板小径；小径上不种树","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1279107097108635649","date":"2020-07-03","text":"Here's a tour of the puzzle pieces that make up #Townscaper. To date, there are 545 of them.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js（sigColor）","note":"模块签名调试色：同一种邻居占用涂同一种颜色","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1277554535297236994","date":"2020-06-29","text":"Ok I'm gonna try something that probably wont work: if you wanna help me translate Townscaper to your language, I simply made the localization spreadsheet public: https:// docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d /1sKbLTWhlpa3CcpOKBnACkJ1kl7_Bi2HvW78gaEQUo1c/edit?usp=sharing …","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1275089608758484992","date":"2020-06-22","text":"It has not escaped some of you that I have yet to release Townscaper. I have an important (secret) business thing to consider, and instead of making a decision I've been making church doors and and ladders. (but do wishlist though: https:// steamcommunity.com/app/1291340 )","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1273520600221433857","date":"2020-06-18","text":"Butterflies fly quite different from birds. Mine loosely orbit a potential landing spot, and drift by randomly switching that spot. Additional world space noise adds variability but also coherence (without boiding) (as always, please wishlist: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ … )","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"落点 = 小花 + 后院；每只绕落点松散转圈（半径 0.12–0.27），3–9 秒随机换附近落点；速度叠世界空间噪声 → 同一片的蝴蝶往同一边飘；翅膀扇动","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1270725616430530566","date":"2020-06-10","text":"You all keep pestering me to release this when I hadn't even added butterflies yet. But do indeed go wishlist: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/1291340/To wnscaper/ …","topic":"life","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1260586697538113537","date":"2020-05-13","text":"Making a trailer is a ton of work. But the good news is I can use the undo/redo stack for snappier and more directed building footage.","topic":"build","status":"game","where":"src/world/app.js","note":"撤销/重做栈（原有）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1259838941299183619","date":"2020-05-11","text":"In code, these are called \"Italian Wires\"","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"从外墙中点沿外法线走 0.6–2.2，碰到另一栋 ≥3 层的房子就拉一根悬链线，每隔 ~0.085 挂一面三角彩旗；整根绳中间摆得最大","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1258421104756097029","date":"2020-05-07","text":"We were long overdue for some splashier splashes","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js","note":"第一块落进水（之前顶层 0）或拆到水面：一圈白色泡沫环向外扩、变淡 + 26 颗飞沫（重力下落、落水即灭）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1258005604066627586","date":"2020-05-06","text":"Here's that but in Townscaper. And Triangular.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1257213678056857600","date":"2020-05-04","text":"Alrighty. First 20 people to reply gets a b e t a k e y *steam on windows for now","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1246074663546916873","date":"2020-04-03","text":"The props now animate when they appear and disappear. This was much trickier than I anticipated.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js","note":"合并网格里没法单独动道具 → 把\"最近 8 次长高的格子\"作为 uniform 交给主材质顶点着色器：格心附近、原高度以上的顶点按弹性曲线从 0.35 长到 1（略过冲）；拆除补一团上飘的灰尘","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1244892370392489989","date":"2020-03-31","text":"Better Birdies: 🐦 More bird shaped 🐦 Only has outlines when sitting 🐦 Shuffle about more 🐦 Has reflections 🐦 Flowier flight","topic":"water","status":"done","where":"src/life/birds.js","note":"海鸥：屋脊顶点找栖位成排停（有描边、会挪步）；起飞 → 绕镇流动地飞（扇翅 / 滑翔）→ 落回空栖位；水里有倒影","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1243228419162341379","date":"2020-03-26","text":"Some moody clouds","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"地平线外一圈放大很多的灰色云 impostor（和树、云共用同一套烘焙）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1242824460325052417","date":"2020-03-25","text":"Finally making some proper UI. Turns out you can make a boring list of buttons playful by just tilting them slightly.","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1241096929490149376","date":"2020-03-20","text":"It has been brought to my attention that not all of you are familiar with my every-other-pixel-is-a-line tech. I make the UVs speed past every 2nd pixel before sampling. It's core to my art style and what lets me get away with one 128² texture and crisp antialiasing up close.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1241046107125399552","date":"2020-03-20","text":"I moved my plants to a 32² corner on the 128² texture I'm using for everything else. Plus they now also use the every-other-pixel-is-a-line tech, so everything is crisp and nice up close","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"植物贴图并进 128² 总图集的 32² 角，并用隔像素一条线的描边技术，近看也清楚；画面：后院沿墙一排圆灌木、矮墙、盆栽树","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1239901715266244609","date":"2020-03-17","text":"If you're hunkered down hiding from the virus (as you should be) and need something to do, I'll be shameless enough to plug our last project, the minimalist strategy game Bad North. Available on PC, Mac, IOs, Android, Switch, PS4, Xbox. @BadNorthGame https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North_Jotunn_Edition/ …","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1238474550511308800","date":"2020-03-13","text":"I needed some more greenery, so now if you build an enclosed area it becomes a backyard!","topic":"build","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"被房子围住、到不了水边的地面层自动变成后院：草坪 + 树","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1237305125070426112","date":"2020-03-10","text":"Obviously, a big benefit of this is that with white finally in my palette, I can properly show off the colored \"bounce\" \"light\" of my custom realtime \"lighting\" system.","topic":"light","status":"game","where":"src/light/bake.js","note":"白墙旁边的红墙会把一点红色反到白墙上","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1237293295887319040","date":"2020-03-10","text":"More colors! I had been assuming the combinatorics would go crazy and that all my assumptions would break if I introduced more colors, but I was wrong and it was fine.","topic":"texture","status":"game","where":"src/core/world.js","note":"15 个色槽（原有）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1215644531221311488","date":"2020-01-10","text":"The technical solution is almost the same as in Bad North. One big difference is that the bright colors wouldn't let me get a way with a monochrome reflection, so I had to figure out this somewhat abstract flat colored mid point. (Also, the wave skirt stretches further this time)","topic":"water","status":"both","where":"src/world/view.js 倒影 / engine","note":"倒影不用单色，而是\"物体色与水色之间的扁平中间色\"；浪裙更宽（浅色光晕）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1215642481162887168","date":"2020-01-10","text":"Ok I went ahead and put this whole project on water. Long time fans of the show know this was inevitable.","topic":"water","status":"game","where":"src/world/view.js","note":"整座城放到水上：石砌基座、浪花、倒影","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1212732478458343424","date":"2020-01-02","text":"Added some flags. Gotta make it homely and welcoming.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/decor.js","note":"每个建筑体量最高的屋脊点（≥3 层，约一半）插杆挂旗；旗面 6×3 细分，顶点着色器沿旗面传播正弦波，朝向顺风","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1210969316071477248","date":"2019-12-28","text":"I've got mom and dad visiting. They've been alternating admiring their new grandchild and building this little town","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1209519206233968641","date":"2019-12-24","text":"A very merry Christmas to you all","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1205422438437273601","date":"2019-12-13","text":"For doors and windows, I use som stencil buffer shenanigans to punch holes in the zbuffer. I admit it was a bit fiddly to figure out.","topic":"build","status":"todo","where":"","note":"模板缓冲给门窗挖洞（现在门窗是贴在墙外的几何）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1205420678859632640","date":"2019-12-13","text":"For the plants, I dug up this ol' trick: alpha is view angle modulated by leaf texture mapped to a sphere.","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"rim = 1-|N·V|，叶片噪声贴在植物自己的坐标上；rim 超过阈值镂空，阈值附近一圈画墨色 → 叶状毛边 + 贴合墨线（替代反向外壳）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1205416648397721601","date":"2019-12-13","text":"New prop placement system! It tries to place as many props as it can without overlap. I use it for doors and windows too, which means they are no longer skewed when placed on skewed tiles, which means skewed tiles now look less awkward.","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js（tryPlace）","note":"门窗按道具放置：尽量多放、互不重叠，开口不随格子歪斜","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1201179450668441600","date":"2019-12-01","text":"Icons!","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1200520827898343425","date":"2019-11-29","text":"DnD hopefulls needn't fear no more, for I've now made the backend of letting you tune your town to your favorite palette.","topic":"texture","status":"game","where":"src/core/world.js","note":"可切换调色板（原有 3 套）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1198957499027795969","date":"2019-11-25","text":"That bit of text up top is the save data for the current construction. I think I've packed the data about as tight as I can. Keeping the save data in a string will make constructions easily shareable between platforms (when it comes to that)","topic":"tools","status":"game","where":"src/world/save.js","note":"存档=字符串，可分享（原有，版本升到 v4 以适配新网格）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1197909675443916803","date":"2019-11-22","text":"Turns out my monitor was too saturated, making me make my colors too dull. This should be better. I've also added some building effects, grass in the gardens, and colored \"bounce\" \"lighting\". I'm real happy even my yellows look good now. Yellows are hard","topic":"light","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"彩色\"反弹光\"（AO 栅格里同时存墙色）、花园草地；屋顶统一陶土色、墙才是调色板颜色","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1195463004919357443","date":"2019-11-15","text":"My brother @mast4461 had a go. Being an engineer he obviously built a nice fractal. Bonus points if you can name it","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1191990107785572352","date":"2019-11-06","text":"Ah, the timeless problem of shrubbery that look good from all angles without too much overdraw. Adding an anchored center vert to the billboards makes them a bit less flat and gives them directionality without messing with the rotation","topic":"life","status":"partial","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"墙根灌木：房子立在同一块台地上时沿墙根种一排；锚定中心点的技巧用在草丛广告牌上","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1190191289922465793","date":"2019-11-01","text":"Trying out some per vertex voxel based shadows. Not great not terrible. Looks better when not moving, and with less contrast, obviously.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1189908238566903808","date":"2019-10-31","text":"However, if you are more careful in providing structural support you'll get curvy brick arches instead and you can build these neat airy cathedral structures","topic":"build","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"两侧（对边）都有支撑时变成拱：半圆拱腹 + 拱肩墙，墙色","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1189902695303458816","date":"2019-10-31","text":"It was real fun making the steel beam support structures. They have this neat artificial yet organic feel to them. Its a place where the WFC algorithm really shines and that would be hard or at least laborious to create with other systems.","topic":"build","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"悬空方块下长深色钢架：角柱 + 横梁 + 斜撑，立在水里的腿有泡沫圈","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1189109278361165825","date":"2019-10-29","text":"I'm happy to announce that at a count of 378 I've now built enough modules to cover all possible cases in whatever funky townscape you might want to build with this.","topic":"build","status":"ref","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"378 个模块覆盖所有情况——确认了\"按角点组合查模块\"的思路，本实现用规则生成几何代替手工模块","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1181464374839521280","date":"2019-10-08","text":"I made some stairs, plus an additional smaller WFC for surface decorations like windows and doors (who's awkward placement otherwise explodes the permutation count) I'll give my first talk on this at Indicade in Paris on the 19th. Hope to see you there! https:// indiecade-europe.eu/en/programme/c onferences …","topic":"build","status":"done","where":"src/build/buildings.js · src/world/navlayer.js","note":"楼梯放在导航图用到的崖脚；门窗另起一层小 WFC：每栋每层一种窗型、一扇门","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1178731576982724611","date":"2019-09-30","text":"I made some grassy plots. I'm real happy with the shapes they make. Eventually, they'll grow some trees and the like.","topic":"life","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"草地块（后院草坪）","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1176516621223043073","date":"2019-09-24","text":"Getting a feel for the style and density of windows. Here you can also see what I'm going for when different colors meet","topic":"build","status":"game","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"窗户的样式和密度：白框小窗，单/双窗，临步道的一面开门","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1174406613031170049","date":"2019-09-18","text":"Today my good friend @podzimcore became the first outsider to take the new project for a spin. Behold the glorious monstrosity he constructed","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1168571866405097472","date":"2019-09-02","text":"A peek at my ambient occlusion approach. The occlusion lives in a layered mesh that's reprojected to a texture at each change. That texture is then blurred, and sampled in the vertex shader of whatever needs lighting.","topic":"light","status":"game","where":"src/light/bake.js","note":"分层遮蔽：每层一张占用栅格 → 盒式模糊两遍 → 每个顶点沿法线外移采样","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1168168400155267072","date":"2019-09-01","text":"Got some very basic lighting in there. Since this ain't proper voxels I had to do a new take on my usual voxel based AO approach","topic":"light","status":"game","where":"src/light/bake.js","note":"不是真体素，所以 AO 也走\"每层栅格\"的办法","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1164926304640229376","date":"2019-08-23","text":"WFC running at interactive speed on that funky grid. Next up is to make it deterministic","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"交互速度的 WFC：目前用规则装配，未实现 WFC","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1163836000688365571","date":"2019-08-20","text":"Basic marching cubes on my funky grid. Next up is turning this into mixed initiative WFC.","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"src/build/buildings.js","note":"不规则网格上的 marching cubes → 现在用规则装配代替 WFC","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1151770831619534848","date":"2019-07-18","text":"I figured out how to make do with relaxation clusters of 3 instead of 7, which means I have to generate fewer unrelaxed patches before I can start relaxing, which makes it faster. Note also that the black and the white grid are *dual* to each other. This is an important concept","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/core/grid.js","note":"松弛按四边形进行；簇大小 3 vs 7 的无限拼接还没做","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1151152046055272449","date":"2019-07-16","text":"Having a look around","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1151137783785771008","date":"2019-07-16","text":"As promised: an aperiodic infinite deterministic irregular relaxed quadrilateral grid.","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/core/grid.js","note":"学到\"非周期、确定性、松弛过的四边形网格\"。目前是单个大 patch（种子固定，可复现），还没做无限延展","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1147881669350891521","date":"2019-07-07","text":"I present: Fairly even irregular quads grid in a hex Todo: 1. Heuristic to reduce (or eliminate) 6 quad verts 2. Tile these babies to infinity","topic":"grid","status":"game","where":"src/core/grid.js","note":"三角形六边形 → 随机两两合并成菱形 → 三角形切 3 格、菱形切 4 格 → 逐格求最佳正方形并松弛。替换了原来\"六边形切 6 个风筝块 + 抖动\"的错误做法","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1120036868966502401","date":"2019-04-21","text":"It's marching squares on irregular quadrilateral grids","topic":"grid","status":"ref","where":"src/core/world.js","note":"不规则四边形上的 marching squares：角点取值决定模块，作为后续模块化的参考","project":"townscaper"},{"id":"1105131621391495176","date":"2019-03-11","text":"Squiggly distance fields, now with animation! Versatile, flexible, but quite laborious","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1104771432440049664","date":"2019-03-10","text":"Squiggly distance fields on mirrored UVs for fast and easy UI decorations. Distance field cutoff can be tweaked separately for borders and center. All one texture, just flipped around a bit. At the start of making @BadNorthGame , UI decoration was a pain, it is now a delight.","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1097458505315946496","date":"2019-02-18","text":"The Viking frontier in @BadNorthGame is dripping with funky math: 1. Triangulate (with some added padding) 2. Walk on triangle edges along each frontier step 3. Bezier sample 4. Tessellate the fields on either side using the bezier and the triangulation","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1092709665199345664","date":"2019-02-05","text":"k-pow !!","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1078792665980915714","date":"2018-12-28","text":"friday night campaign map node graffing","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1063115611289645057","date":"2018-11-15","text":"Like many of you have suggested, I finally added grass to slopes to make navigability easier to read (especially on overcast levels where the lighting ain't helping much). I'm happy enough with the result to ditch the previous white dotted lines. https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North/ …","topic":"light","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"坡面（邻居高度不同的顶面）草丛密度是平地的 2 倍多","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1062374549407350790","date":"2018-11-13","text":"To make Bad North even prettier, I'm adding some extra smoothing to the island using my voxel normals. It helps break up the grid and make it all look a wee bit more natural. (also, go wishlist @BadNorthGame on Steam: https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North/ … )","topic":"grid","status":"done","where":"src/core/meshwriter.js","note":"Bad North 用体素法线做额外平滑：这里软三角形在同一位置按夹角(<55°)平均法线 → 弯崖壁圆润、崖顶边仍硬","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1061229717582475264","date":"2018-11-10","text":"But you can break up that repetition by using a few different ones with different settings (all still using the same texture)","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1061227418961219585","date":"2018-11-10","text":"Obviously, if you stretch it too far, you will start to notice the repetition","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1061221291137605633","date":"2018-11-10","text":"I'm writing a simple graphic for UI decoration. A single texture can be oriented 8 different ways and mirrors around the center to work in any size. (also, Bad North drops on Steam Nov 16 https:// store.steampowered.com/app/688420/Bad _North/ … )","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1056999668486471682","date":"2018-10-29","text":"Works well in daylight too, largely thanks to the max blend","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1056992291108413446","date":"2018-10-29","text":"Oh no! I made an error! The quads above shrink way more than they are supposed to. This looks much better and breaks up the flame in a much more interesting way:","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1056990611738451968","date":"2018-10-29","text":"New fire effect. For blend mode, I use Max instead of Add to have better control over my colors and to make the particles blend together and form a common silhouette.","topic":"texture","status":"done","where":"src/life/effects.js","note":"烟囱口发射软圆粒子，黄 → 橙 → 红；混合方程 MaxEquation：重叠处取最大值而不是相加 → 融成一个轮廓、白天也不发白（1056999668486471682）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1042732450730913793","date":"2018-09-20","text":"The graph generator I ended up using for the Bad North campaign maps: 1. Create nodes of varying sizes and spread them out 2. Cull nodes outside bounds 3. Do a random walk from start to finish 4. Do some more random walks 5. Pick some more random nodes","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1024679338292256769","date":"2018-08-01","text":"Some UI flair","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1022855252574437376","date":"2018-07-27","text":"it's my birthday!","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1022573208590057472","date":"2018-07-26","text":"The look and feel of the basic meat and potato melee combat is one of the things I'm most proud of in Bad North","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1017355723171344385","date":"2018-07-12","text":"Making some thicker outlines for all you 4k high ballers out there","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1016680972610359298","date":"2018-07-10","text":"This is what the confirm popup looks like:","topic":"tools","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015151731804721152","date":"2018-07-06","text":"I change the mip level of the noise texture throughout the smoke trail. This aids the transition from crisp at the base to blurry a the tip","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015149712469524480","date":"2018-07-06","text":"I only sample my noise texture once per quad, but I scroll the UVs randomly forward or backward along the flow of the smoke. This further breaks up the recognizability of individual blobs and it creates some of that cool multi layered flow feeling thick smoke should have","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015142746372366336","date":"2018-07-06","text":"I solve the problems of z-depth and draw order by drawing the effect in 2 passes. The first pass is black, and and has a full alpha ner the base. The second pass is lighter, more transparent towards the base, and has its cutoff pulled in 1 pixel (creating the crisp outline)","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1015140880666300416","date":"2018-07-06","text":"Smoke effect. A full billowy base tied together by a crisp outline seamlessly transitioned to a blurry fade. The effect is probably a bit much for my current purposes, but I think it solves some interesting problems so I wanted to share it","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1010979395719319552","date":"2018-06-24","text":"A selection of the many handsome faces you might come across in @BadNorthGame","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587828992266240","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587825024425984","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587821220229120","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587817021636609","date":"2018-06-15","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"1007587812462530561","date":"2018-06-15","text":"Proper games have waterfalls. I'm glad to report that @BadNorthGame is now a proper game.","topic":"water","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"999191760944418817","date":"2018-05-23","text":"Adding the option of disabling gore made me realized just how much I rely on blood for environmental storytelling. I should probably start asking some questions about what kind of person I am and what kind of art I put into this world.","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"999185422403055616","date":"2018-05-23","text":"For my blood splatter UVs, I'm interpolating between sprite-space and skin-space using the fwidth of skin UV. This gives me a sprite-space map on the tummy (where the skin UVs are static) while the splatter on the face follows the actual motion of the head.","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"995043346778415104","date":"2018-05-11","text":"The pathfinding in some levels does get a bit convoluted","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"995034777756536833","date":"2018-05-11","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"987267068495003648","date":"2018-04-20","text":"Using inspector expressions, I can live tweak the cost function of my projectile trajectory lookup tables. Very handy.","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"984813819280191488","date":"2018-04-13","text":"Blood soaking as a health indicator for the big fellas and a proper stun state for the little ones","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"984703192465330176","date":"2018-04-13","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"978211952504852480","date":"2018-03-26","text":"Pro tip: use fwidth, ddx and ddy to create crisp, pixel perfect, zoom independent, antialiased lines with your shaders. https:// computergraphics.stackexchange.com/questions/61/w hat-is-fwidth-and-how-does-it-work …","topic":"texture","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"978195201901711360","date":"2018-03-26","text":"Some of it will have to wait for some later project","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"978194866520944641","date":"2018-03-26","text":"Some of it looks very similar","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"974579499802202113","date":"2018-03-16","text":"For a given position, Barycentric Coordinates can be calculated with 1 subtraction and 1 dot product (if you've precalculated some nice vectors in the triangle)","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"974564862729838592","date":"2018-03-16","text":"I'm making some pedagogical gizmos for my GDC microtalk, like this illustration of Barycentric Coordinates. Gizmos > powerpoints.","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"974325184525201409","date":"2018-03-15","text":"We were having strange crashes when using Unity's Physics.OverlapBox. We solved it (hopefully) by making our own box-box test in two incredibly stressful hours. Behold, our beautiful viking raid planner:","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"972829402873716737","date":"2018-03-11","text":"If you're heading to GDC, come see my microtalk about the triangular flow fields we use for pathfinding and combat http:// schedule.gdconf.com/session/tech-t oolbox/854263 …","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"969860566322958336","date":"2018-03-03","text":"My unit sprites have 1 direction, so they need to be directionally ambiguous. They are mostly symmetrical and avoid features that feel jarring when they flip. Would these sword tips be axe heads, you would notice at a glance that they are pointing in two distinct directions","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"959752525867036672","date":"2018-02-03","text":"A great unexpected joy in this project has been writing my own navmesh. It's an oddly relaxing job full of small and approachable math-puzzles. Here you see some pulsating vertex cells; a dual to the triangular grid and a suitable place to start with foliage placement.","topic":"grid","status":"partial","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"落点：按顶面类型 + 变形后的多边形随机取点（还没用顶点格做对偶）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"959530111187013632","date":"2018-02-02","text":"I've been tweaking the foliage system today. It now supports multiple grass types per level.","topic":"life","status":"done","where":"src/life/vegetation.js","note":"两套草色：普通草顶面 / 崖边干草","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"958410200146497537","date":"2018-01-30","text":"The approach is versatile enough that I can use it for the ingame banners too","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"958371606350454784","date":"2018-01-30","text":"The beginnings of a portrait generator. It currently runs on 5 examples (all male and with a similar hierarchy) but it's content agnostic and should support a diverse set of inputs.","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"946660607008403456","date":"2017-12-29","text":"While @rtm223 is away on holiday I'm taking some time to focus on the important things, like making blood, corpses and arrows stick to boats and adding pretty little flowers","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"Bad North 战斗：长船靠岸、箭雨、滩上尸体和血；血、尸体、箭射中后粘在船上随船移动。原文末尾顺带提了小花，画面里几乎看不到。（之前误记成「小花」，已更正）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"943230624369868800","date":"2017-12-19","text":"And yeah, obviously the snow flakes are affected by the wind system and thus flow around the island","topic":"terrain","status":"done","where":"src/life/atmosphere.js","note":"3000 片雪沿风场平流 + 下落 + 飘摆；落进地面 / 出界从上风边重新生成；开雪时主材质朝上的面混白（台地、屋顶积雪）","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"943230620242796544","date":"2017-12-19","text":"I'm heading north for a few days to see the folks. In the meantime, here's some seasonally relevant hype material for @BadNorthGame :","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"938422757288792064","date":"2017-12-06","text":"I'm extra happy with how the grouping turned out. It's a sort of cellular automaton where nodes get eaten by the neighbor group to which they are most connected. Here's a slowmo to illustrate:","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"938405900573986816","date":"2017-12-06","text":"A more legible peek at the campaign generation for @BadNorthGame . Islands get spread apart and divided into regions.","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"938395867215728640","date":"2017-12-06","text":"Node graph programming is by far the most delightful programming","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"931196707236392960","date":"2017-11-16","text":"My generated levels all keep a virtual voxel space. It is used for light baking, soft normals, various 3D textures, simplified collision, wind simulation etc.","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"929417420921556993","date":"2017-11-11","text":"Fun fact: I generate smooth normals for all my meshes and use a blend between smooth and hard normals in the final lighting","topic":"light","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"926903893866541057","date":"2017-11-04","text":"Here is what my wind vectors look like. They can be used by all kinds of systems, including shaders","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/life/atmosphere.js","note":"每层一张 2D 网格：实心格栅格化再模糊 = 阻挡度 b；风 = 基础风向去掉\"撞向障碍物\"的法向分量（贴边只剩切向）、贴边加速、被挡住往上抬；sample(x,y,z) 三线性；面板「风场箭头」显示两层箭头","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"926890207298899969","date":"2017-11-04","text":"Not really. I build a custom mesh for the flag using a bezier curve along virtual wind particles","topic":"life","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"926834721392340992","date":"2017-11-04","text":"The banners where due for a makeover. I built a wind system to get them flapping just right","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"917405214638006273","date":"2017-10-09","text":"A somewhat major breakthrough in my procedural generation: a heuristic for deliberately generating navigable levels","topic":"grid","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"913407568730615808","date":"2017-09-28","text":"Ok, I'm proud of this one. Can any of you brainy nerds figure out what we're looking at here?","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"912691357440978945","date":"2017-09-26","text":"Long time no combat gifs","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"911913981731885056","date":"2017-09-24","text":"I'm looking at the campaign map. Saving island snapshots to 64² textures and then crisping them back up with some shader magic","topic":"terrain","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"906425294533394432","date":"2017-09-09","text":"It's like navigating a Swiss cheese","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"906416813810049025","date":"2017-09-09","text":"New cave tileset. These levels really challenge your spacial skills #screenshotsaturday #madewithunity @BadNorthGame","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"906207980802252801","date":"2017-09-08","text":"I've been working on some new fog (sped up in the gif). For background effects, subtlety is key.","topic":"fx","status":"done","where":"src/life/atmosphere.js","note":"岛周围一张大圆盘，alpha 随半径 smoothstep 增大、叠两层缓慢流动的噪声，颜色取背景色偏白 —— 背景效果，宁淡勿浓","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"903647529203634176","date":"2017-09-01","text":"Spears are so weird to implement. I can see why most games don't use them","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"902103473365417984","date":"2017-08-28","text":"Ok, one more visualization. Distances this time. I really should get back to proper work now","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"902069261304287232","date":"2017-08-28","text":"Just for fun: visualization of data inheritance in my flow/distance/influence fields","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"901842167508992000","date":"2017-08-27","text":"Made my flow/influence fields even smarter: In addition to distance and direction to nearest unit, it can now tell you what type they are","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"901469409579061248","date":"2017-08-26","text":"Working on nicer ship wakes","topic":"water","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"880853661936734211","date":"2017-06-30","text":"Units got stuck when meeting in narrow passages. I fixed it by introducing left handed traffic. Never felt so clever.","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"877995885250138119","date":"2017-06-22","text":"（帖子无文字说明）","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"870558914345041921","date":"2017-06-02","text":"I think we've all had days like this","topic":"show","status":"na","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"},{"id":"870296307889573889","date":"2017-06-01","text":"Units can now get knocked off ledges","topic":"fx","status":"todo","where":"","note":"","project":"badnorth"}]};
